.TH DURATION 1 "April 2026" "@udlearn/duration" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duration \- interpret numeric time spans as human\-readable durations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duration
.RB [ \-s | \-m | \-l ]
.RB [ \-\-json | \-\-table ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR unit " | " \-\-unit = unit ]
.RI < value " .\|.\|.\|>"
.br
.B duration
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B duration
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B duration
reads one or more numeric values and prints each as a duration in days, hours, minutes, seconds, and milliseconds.
Values are interpreted in
.B milliseconds
unless
.B \-\-unit
or the
.B DURATION_UNIT
environment variable selects another scale (see
.BR UNITS ).
.PP
This manual documents the standalone implementations (POSIX shell and optional static binary). The npm package also ships a Node\-based CLI with the same flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s
Short format (e.g.\&
.BR "1h 30m" ).
.TP
.BR \-m
Medium format (e.g.\&
.BR "1 hr 30 mins" ).
.TP
.BR \-l
Long format (e.g.\&
.BR "1 hour 30 minutes" ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print each value as a JSON object with total
.BR milliseconds ,
.BR seconds ,
.BR minutes ,
.BR hours ,
and
.B days
(floating\-point totals, same as the library\(cqs
.BR toJson() ).
.TP
.B \-\-table
Print a table of those fields for all values.
.TP
.BI \-u " unit" ", " \-\-unit = unit
Input unit for every positional value (default
.BR ms ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit 0.
.PP
More than one of
.BR \-s ", " \-m ", " \-l
may be given; each selected format is applied in order, one line per value per format (see
.BR EXAMPLES ).
.SH UNITS
Recognized unit names (case\-insensitive) include:
.BR ms ", " milli ", " millis ", " millisecond ", " milliseconds ;
.BR s ", " sec ", " secs ", " second ", " seconds ;
.BR m ", " min ", " mins ", " minute ", " minutes ;
.BR h ", " hr ", " hrs ", " hour ", " hours ;
.BR d ", " day ", " days .
Unknown unit names fall back to milliseconds.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DURATION_UNIT
Default input unit when
.B \-\-unit
is not set.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interpret two values as milliseconds (default short format):
.PP
.nf
$ duration 3600 54000
3s 600ms
54s
.fi
.PP
Medium format:
.PP
.nf
$ duration \-m 3600
3 secs 600 ms
.fi
.PP
Long format with values given in seconds:
.PP
.nf
$ duration \-l \-\-unit=s 3600
1 hour
.fi
.PP
Negative values are shown as a positive duration followed by
.BR \(dq ago \(dq :
.PP
.nf
$ duration \-s \-500
500ms ago
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
.SS Static binary (Linux, macOS, Windows)
Use the installer (set
.B PREFIX
to change the install directory, default
.BR ~/.local/bin ):
.PP
.nf
curl \-fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/udlearn/duration/main/install.sh | sh
.fi
.PP
Or download a release archive for your OS and architecture from the project releases page and place the
.B duration
executable on your
.BR PATH .
.SS POSIX shell script
Copy
.B scripts/duration
from the repository, mark it executable
.RB ( chmod +x ),
and run it with a POSIX
.B sh
that provides
.BR awk
(e.g.\& Linux, macOS, Git Bash, MSYS2, or WSL).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR awk (1).
.PP
npm package:
.UR https://www.npmjs.com/package/@udlearn/duration
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Ralph Florent and contributors.
